{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey Security Deposit Law cap, interest and return deadline","requirement":"A landlord may not demand more than one and one-half months' rent as a security deposit, may raise it by no more than 10% a year, and must return the deposit with interest within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; annual increase max 10%","coverage_conditions":"Residential rentals in New Jersey where the landlord collects a security deposit; collecting one is optional, but if collected these rules apply. Deposit-account rules exclude seasonal rentals of 125 days or fewer.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential tenancies; deposit-account rules exclude seasonal rentals of 125 days or fewer."},"exemptions":"Seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days by a person whose permanent residence is elsewhere; seasonal, temporary or migrant farm worker housing is not seasonal use.","penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount wrongly withheld plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees if the deposit is not returned within 30 days.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Safe Housing Act security deposit return after domestic violence termination","requirement":"When a tenant ends a lease early under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available within 15 business days and give written notice within three business days.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a lease under the Safe Housing Act after documenting domestic violence or threat of harm; the law does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Leases terminated early under the Safe Housing Act; not transient or seasonal rentals."},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
